$ graphify install --project --platform codebuddy
  references       ->  .codebuddy/skills/graphify/references
  skill installed  ->  .codebuddy/skills/graphify/SKILL.md
  CODEBUDDY.md     ->  created at <FIXTURE_ROOT>/home/.codebuddy/CODEBUDDY.md

Project-scoped install. Add to version control:
  git add .codebuddy/

Done. Open your AI coding assistant and type:

  /graphify .

Prefer a hosted version? Try the graphify platform free for 14 days:
https://app.graphify.com


$ graphify codebuddy install
  references       ->  <FIXTURE_ROOT>/home/.codebuddy/skills/graphify/references
  skill installed  ->  <FIXTURE_ROOT>/home/.codebuddy/skills/graphify/SKILL.md
graphify section written to <FIXTURE_ROOT>/project/CODEBUDDY.md
  .codebuddy/settings.json  ->  PreToolUse hooks registered

CodeBuddy will now check the knowledge graph before answering
codebase questions and rebuild it after code changes.
